quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  6,119,"Why should you not eat from (the meat of) that (animal) over which Allah’s name is invoked (at the time of slaughter), while He has already explained to you whatever He has forbidden you, except for what you are highly compelled (to eat)? Indeed, many people mislead (others) with their desires without (any concrete) knowledge. Indeed, your Lord is He Who knows the transgressors well."
  6,120,"Abandon the outward sins and the inward ones. Indeed, those who commit sins shall be recompensed for what they used to commit."
  6,121,"And do not eat from (the meat of) that (animal) over which Allah’s name has not been invoked (at the time of slaughter). It is indeed a disobedience (contravening the Sacred Law). Indeed, the devils inspire their intimate friends to argue with you. And if you obey them, you will also become polytheists."
  6,122,"Can the one who was dead, then We gave him life and provided him with a light, with which he walks among the people (to enlighten them), be comparable to the one (trapped) in manifold darkness, which he cannot escape? Thus, whatever (misdeeds) the disbelievers used to do were made alluring to them."
  6,123,"Thus, We have made the powerful ones the criminals in every town so that they may devise their (evil) plots therein. But they only plot against themselves, though they are unaware."
  6,124,"And when a revelation comes to them, they say: ‘We will never believe unless we are given the like of what was given to the messengers of Allah.’ Allah knows best where to place His message. Soon, humiliation before Allah and severe punishment shall befall the guilty because of the plots they used to devise."
